WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.356 --> 00:00:11.421
Norbert Weiner was a famous professor.

2
00:00:12.021 --> 00:00:13.942
He was a very intelligent man.

3
00:00:14.642 --> 00:00:17.143
However, he was very forgetful.

4
00:00:20.564 --> 00:00:24.146
One day, the Weiner family was moving to another house.

5
00:00:25.086 --> 00:00:28.648
Mrs. Weiner knew that her husband wouldn't be much help moving.

6
00:00:29.468 --> 00:00:34.011
So she sent him to school while she and the movers worked together.

7
00:00:36.693 --> 00:00:41.777
Mrs. Weiner was sure that Professor Weiner would forget that they had moved.

8
00:00:42.517 --> 00:00:45.499
She wrote down their new address on a piece of paper.

9
00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:51.143
She gave it to him and said, "Honey, this is our new address.

10
00:00:51.923 --> 00:00:53.104
Don't forget!"

11
00:00:53.124 --> 00:01:00.582
"All right, darling," replied Professor Weiner as he kissed his wife good-bye.

12
00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:06.046
"Good-bye, and have a nice day at school," said Mrs.

13
00:01:06.106 --> 00:01:12.531
Weiner. While at school, Professor Weiner had a great idea.

14
00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:16.955
He decided to write it down in case he forgot it.

15
00:01:17.775 --> 00:01:21.558
He reached into his pocket and took out a piece of paper.

16
00:01:24.481 --> 00:01:26.943
He wrote his idea down with a pencil.

17
00:01:27.623 --> 00:01:32.271
But of course, it was the piece of paper with his new address on it!

18
00:01:34.973 --> 00:01:38.716
Later, Professor Weiner looked at the piece of paper again.

19
00:01:39.537 --> 00:01:40.938
He read his idea.

20
00:01:41.679 --> 00:01:45.582
He decided it wasn't very good and threw the paper away.

21
00:01:46.363 --> 00:01:50.927
And yes, it was the piece of paper with the new address on it!

22
00:01:53.989 --> 00:01:56.872
At the end of the day, he left for home.

23
00:01:57.652 --> 00:01:59.253
He went to his old address.

24
00:02:00.074 --> 00:02:03.317
He completely forgot that his family had moved.

25
00:02:05.518 --> 00:02:07.700
When he got there, the house was empty.

26
00:02:08.421 --> 00:02:11.283
He thought about the piece of paper from that morning.

27
00:02:12.104 --> 00:02:14.005
He remembered that he threw it away.

28
00:02:14.706 --> 00:02:17.948
But he couldn't remember the address that was written on it.

29
00:02:19.009 --> 00:02:21.591
He thought and thought about what to do.

30
00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:27.016
The sun had set and he was very worried.

31
00:02:28.012 --> 00:02:32.014
Fortunately, he noticed a young girl playing behind the house.

32
00:02:34.076 --> 00:02:40.959
He walked over to the girl in the darkness and said, "Excuse me, I'm Norbert Weiner and my

33
00:02:41.039 --> 00:02:42.220
family has just moved.

34
00:02:43.041 --> 00:02:44.862
Maybe you know where we've moved to?"

35
00:02:47.163 --> 00:02:50.605
The young girl replied, "Yes, Daddy.

36
00:02:51.345 --> 00:02:52.986
Mommy knew you would forget.

37
00:02:53.927 --> 00:02:55.428
I'll take you home now."
